                <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="2" fill="currentColor" />
                <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity=".55" />
                <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="7.4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity=".28" />
              </svg>
              The assistant
            </p>
            <h2 id="mcp-h">Ask your <em class="em">own</em> questions.</h2>
            <p class="lede">
              The Mac app ships a read-only MCP server over the database your phone keeps current,
              so a question costs a lookup rather than a re-parse of a stale XML export. It cannot
              change or delete anything.
            </p>
            <p class="caveat">
              <strong>The honest caveat:</strong> a cloud assistant may upload whatever it reads.
              That is the assistant's behaviour, not Hozz's — which is a good reason to point a
              local one at it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="tiny">What it can read</h3>
